October 23, 2012

DSS is pleased to announce DACS version 1.4.28.  DACS, a light-weight single
sign-on and role-based security system for Apache or server-based software,
provides comprehensive authentication capabilities, and powerful, transparent
rule-based authorization checking for any web service or CGI program.
It runs on recent Linux, FreeBSD, and Mac OS X platforms and is distributed
under an open source license.

DACS is a light-weight single sign-on and role-based access control system
for web servers and server-based software.  For release notes, download links,
checksums, and errata, please visit:
    http://dacs.dss.ca/download.html

All DACS installations are urged to upgrade.  This release may require
some minor configuration changes - refer to the distribution's HISTORY file
for details.

For more information, please visit the DACS home page at http://dacs.dss.ca.

